e current recommendation (could stay with C or change). Must refer to existing discussion, use explicit facts, explain implications. We have our own notes: C strengths and concerns. Also we have Agent 1's observations about A's crew cooperation and adaptability (A positive crew atmosphere, but egocentric, not willing to further education). Also Agent 1 said B uncooperative, D arrogant.\n\nAgent 3 argued that C is unfriendly (but that was not in our notes; we have \"C is regarded as a show\u2011off\" and \"not open to new ideas\". Show\u2011off could be perceived as unfriendly. So we can address that.\n\nWe need to decide whether to keep vote for C or shift. Let's evaluate: C strengths: anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. Concerns: show\u2011off, not open to new ideas (feedback). Also we have no info on attention/accuracy. A strengths: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, understands technology, positive crew atmosphere. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Also we have no explicit reliability evidence beyond \"creates positive atmosphere\". But we have \"A keeps calm in a crisis\" and \"A can make correct decisions quickly\". Also \"A understands complicated technology\". So A has strong decision quality, stress resilience, technical competence, crew cooperation (positive atmosphere). Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe manageable.\n\nC's leadership is strong, but show\u2011off and not open to new ideas could affect crew cooperation and adaptability. A's egocentric and communication difficulty also affect crew cooperation and professional communication.\n\nWhich is stronger? The panel must consider all criteria. Both have concerns. We need to argue.\n\nWe could propose that Candidate C remains best because anticipation and technical insight are critical for long-distance, and leadership outweighs show\u2011off, and adaptability can be coached. Or we could shift to A because crew cooperation is proven and decision speed is crucial.\n\nGiven Agent 3's shift, we can either agree or argue. Let's decide to maintain C, but address concerns: show\u2011off and not open to new ideas may be mitigated, and A's communication difficulty may be more severe. Provide evidence: C's anticipation of dangerous situations (stress resilience), sees complex connections (technical), leadership (crew cooperation). A's egocentric and communication difficulty may impair crew coordination, especially on long flights.\n\nThus we will keep vote for C, argue that strengths outweigh concerns, and that A's communication issues are more safety-critical.\n\nWe must reference Agent 1's observations: A creates positive atmosphere but egocentric and not willing to further education. Also Agent 3's claim about C being unfriendly; we can counter that show\u2011off is not necessarily unfriendly, and leadership is strong.\n\nThus produce public message: \"I understand Agent 3's concerns, but I still recommend C because ...\"\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
